"type":"text"},{"text":"starting with the eighth note beam using a number attribute of 1.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBeam","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that the beam number does not distinguish sets of beams that overlap, as it does for slur and other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements. Beaming groups are distinguished by being in different voices and\/or the presence or absence of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"grace and cue elements.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Beams that have a begin value can also have a fan attribute to indicate accelerandos and ritardandos using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fanned beams. The fan attribute may also be used with a continue value if the fanning direction changes on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that note. The value is “none” if not specified.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The repeater attribute has been deprecated in MusicXML 3.0. Formerly used for tremolos, it needs to be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified with a “yes” value for each beam using it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<beam>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbeam"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","title":"Swift.Equatable"},"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorM